  "originalQuery": "You are managing a Cloud Spanner database for a logistics company. Shipment details are stored in a table called shipments , and the table has columns shipmentId , customerId , and destination . The management frequently queries shipments with destination='New York' for different customers. To improve performance and maintain query flexibility, you decide to parameterize the query. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. SELECT shipmentId FROM shipments WHERE customerId=@customerId AND destination='New York'<br/>B. SELECT shipmentId FROM shipments WHERE customerId LIKE @customerId AND destination=@destination<br/>C. SELECT shipmentId FROM shipments WHERE customerId=@customerId OR destination='New York'<br/>D. SELECT shipmentId FROM shipments WHERE customerId=@customerId AND destination=@destination",
